OL,3,ARecord 5,200 heat-linked deaths        
OL,4,Aestimated in England this year         
OL,6,FMore than 5,000 people suffered        
OL,7,Fheat-associated deaths in England this 
OL,8,Fsummer, the UK Health Security Agency  
OL,9,F(UKHSA) has estimated - the highest    
OL,10,Fnumber since records began in 2016.    
OL,12,FThe UK experienced its hottest summer  
OL,13,Fon record in 2026, and the estimated   
OL,14,F5,258 heat-linked deaths were twice the
OL,15,Fprevious high of 2,985 in 2022.        
OL,17,FThe most deadly period of the year for 
OL,18,Fheat-related deaths was between 21 and 
OL,19,F28 June, when there were an estimated  
OL,20,F2,401 heat-associated deaths.          
OL,21,FTemperatures peaked at 38C in that     
OL,22,Fperiod.                                
OL,23,APub: 24-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2 
